<BaseLayout seo={{title:'Editorial Policy — GAME//BRIEF',description:'How GAME//BRIEF sources, writes, edits and corrects its gaming journalism.',path:'/editorial-policy'}}><section class="container max-w-3xl py-10"><p class="kicker">Trust</p><h1 class="text-5xl font-black">Editorial Policy</h1><div class="prose-gb mt-6"><p>This policy explains how GAME//BRIEF approaches news gathering, reviews and guides, and what readers can expect from our coverage.</p><h2>Editorial independence</h2><p>Coverage decisions at GAME//BRIEF are made by our editorial team, led by site owner activex, independently of advertisers, publishers, platform holders or other commercial partners. Advertising never determines what we cover or how we cover it.</p><h2>Sourcing and accuracy</h2><p>We aim to verify claims before publishing and to be clear about what is confirmed fact versus rumor or speculation. Where we rely on outside reporting, we credit the original source and link to it where possible.</p><h2>Reviews</h2><p>Game reviews reflect the honest opinion of the author after reasonable time with the game. Review copies or early access provided by publishers do not influence the outcome or content of a review.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>When we get something wrong, we correct it. Significant corrections are noted on the affected article. If you spot an error, email us at <a href="mailto:officialbeyondsense@gmail.com">officialbeyondsense@gmail.com</a> with the article link and details.</p><h2>Authorship</h2><p>Every article is attributed to the author who wrote it. Our current writing team consists of three authors working under activex; you can see each author's full body of work on their <a href="/authors">author page</a>.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
